rived; and, veiled in moonlight, appears the moon in the heavens.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.973,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-119-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2111009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d6bd0e13a962075b66a34844ebe6e6d94574589298b046fe9a5f2581027c6f14","compact":"6ec921b0b08898821833ca9569256bc0413595a5271509c6c82ebb5d229104a8","nasal":"23f69ccbd23bd3b3966bfa42cb4e449bedbc51ac35a9c068d57ed3e80ba4a4aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-111-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":111,"verse":10,"english":"Go you; I permit you. Do you seek the society of Rāma. I have been pleased with your sweet converse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-119-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2111010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"502a4a4bc4850b47243b12e06a8e4af8b8f4b5dc7122a04f08242fb179083595","compact":"5104e510796203a5317436054200cef06d15464c5c0164ac858c1e2a1b4c0f7a","nasal":"25bc5a644384d7c715da8ac128765ff060a2904e03aff63811418563d5eb2772"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-111-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":111,"verse":11,"english":"O daughter of Mithilā, do you deck yourself before me. Do you thus please me, my child, you that look beautiful with excellent ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-119-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2111011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4d6778b9dc36aceff8463b104916c964ba9c26f7bf393379ec83c6902cbcee5c","compact":"0f09e5edc7a4188ecb63fbe00f89101e8c8eaeb859f082fa5e5719a75dfaf8cb","nasal":"0f09e5edc7a4188ecb63fbe00f89101e8c8eaeb859f082fa5e5719a75dfaf8cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-111-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":111,"verse":12,"english":"Thereat, having adorned herself, Sītā, resembling the daughter of a celestial, bowing down to the feet (of the female ascetic), directed her steps towards Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-119-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2111012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"55a8b2c11d570682e1bf285cffe98b02ae2751a1c02bb0b338977d84e11044e5","compact":"0ec29583a19e9756bc972a2dd4ed2dd177c57e051e301588fe0f24124d18ac96","nasal":"0ec29583a19e9756bc972a2dd4ed2dd177c57e051e301588fe0f24124d18ac96"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-111-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":111,"verse":13,"english":"And that best of speakers, Raghava, saw Sita, decked with the ornaments affectionately presented by the ascetic; and he rejoiced thereat.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-119-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2111013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7eec12124f6e78d07bf567cb928e23788806de7bdec1d7bf7e103359986f4d48","compact":"97263e54c95e56706a3296d7ab54fdfa3cdb89c54134cd9f06c3e0a32b44309e","nasal":"97263e54c95e56706a3296d7ab54fdfa3cdb89c54134cd9f06c3e0a32b44309e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-111-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":111,"verse":14,"english":"Then Mithila's daughter, Sita, related to Rama all about her having been affectionately presented by the ascetic with attire, ornaments and the garland.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-119-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2111014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d47966af4ce26cb841cace74958a55003926e33126b1b059b8122b823612ee2d","compact":"10a5309588bd49f2d8a7c655ddb9